-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration site. You can read the news without creating an account. Please use demo credentials and never reuse a password from another service.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account forms</h2>
+    <p>Sign-in and sign-up ask only for a username and password. A pseudonym is sufficient; we do not ask for your real name, email address, phone number, or date of birth. These details are sent only when you submit the form, to sign in or create an account.</p>
+    <p>Submitting sends those two fields over HTTPS to our external account service hosted on Google Cloud Functions at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api/login</code> or <code>/times_cdn/api/register</code>. That service also receives connection information such as your IP address. The app's JavaScript request omits cookies and referrer information and does not follow redirects.</p>
+    <p>The app does not put credentials or returned tokens in local storage, session storage, or cookies. It clears the password field after each completed submission attempt. Your browser's password manager may offer to save credentials under your control.</p>
+    <p>This demo does not provide account access, correction, or deletion controls. The external account service's retention and deletion practices are not specified in this project, so we cannot promise a retention period or automatic deletion. Do not submit personal or sensitive information.</p>
+
+    <h2>Optional third-party resources</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load analytics or advertising scripts, Google Fonts, or third-party preconnections. It uses fonts installed on your device. Account details are not used by this app for analytics or advertising.</p>
+    <p>Some news pages contain images hosted by third parties, including Imgur and Google Cloud Run. Loading those resources exposes connection information to their hosts. The site uses a no-referrer policy so page addresses are not sent as referrers. Links to external websites connect to those websites when you follow them.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and cookies</h2>
+    <p>A reading-list session is saved when you choose to bookmark an article, rather than being created just for browsing. It contains saved article identifiers and may use a session cookie to associate the list with your browser. Clearing this site's cookies disconnects your browser from that list; it does not guarantee deletion of server-side records.</p>
+    <p>Some articles demonstrate DevTools debugging scenarios and may set test cookies or make requests to demonstration APIs. For example, the plant statistics example creates test cache cookies for its API path. These examples are separate from account credentials.</p>
+
+    <h2>Browser privacy boundaries</h2>
+    <p>Document responses request no browser or shared-cache storage. Response headers also disable camera, microphone, location, motion sensor, and browsing-topics access where supported. Hosting infrastructure and external services may maintain their own request logs; their retention is not configured by this app.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
